 button moves exactly one phase forward in the cycle, once per press (holding the button does not keep stepping; bounces shorter than 30 ms do not count as extra presses)."},{"id":"C4","text":"The lights only glow when the room is dark (A0 reading below 300). When the room is bright (A0 reading above 340), all four lights are off, and they come back showing the current phase when it gets dark again."},{"id":"C5","text":"The button still steps the phase while the room is bright; the new phase shows once the room is dark."},{"id":"C6","text":"Between readings of 300 and 340 the lamp keeps its previous on/off state, so it doesn't flicker at the boundary."}],"assumptions":["'Next day's phase' is simplified to the next of the 8 classic moon phases per press, since four lights can only show 8 distinct shapes.","The moon is shown as seen from the northern hemisphere: it grows from the right and shrinks from the right.","Light sensor: photoresistor from 5V to A0, 10 kΩ from A0 to GND, so a darker room gives a lower A0 reading.","Dark below a reading of 300, bright again above 340 (the bench calibrates both). At power-up the lamp counts as dark only if the reading is below 300.","The phase is not remembered after power-off; it starts at full moon each time.","Four yellow LEDs with 220 Ω resistors draw about 14 mA each, about 56 mA total."]},"lines":[{"t":"hello","fw":"vibread-bench","proto":1,"design":"0068958b","board":"uno-r3-atmega328p-5v"},{"t":"begin","test":"rails.vcc"},{"t":"vcc","mv":5001},{"t":"end","test":"rails.vcc","status":"pass"},{"t":"begin","test":"pins.readonly"},{"t":"read","pin":"D2","pull":0,"ones":0,"n":32},{"t":"read","pin":"D2","pull":1,"ones":0,"n":32},{"t":"read","pin":"D3","pull":0,"ones":0,"n":32},{"t":"read","pin":"D3","pull":1,"ones":0,"n":32},{"t":"read","pin":"D4","pull":0,"ones":0,"n":32},{"t":"read","pin":"D4","pull":1,"ones":0,"n":32},{"t":"read","pin":"D5","pull":0,"ones":0,"n":32},{"t":"read","pin":"D5","pull":1,"ones":0,"n":32},{"t":"read